# Line endings are part of the source, not of the checkout.
#
# Several things in this tree read a repository file with `include_str!` and
# then match against `\n`-terminated literals: `src/ffi/header.rs` compares
# `include/rsemu.h` byte-for-byte against what `src/ffi/abi.rs` generates, and
# `fw::pcbios::tests::add_second_processor` rewrites `machines/pc-at.machine`
# by searching for whole object blocks. A checkout that converted those files
# to CRLF broke all three on `windows-latest` while passing everywhere else,
# and the header test's own message — "one file is a prefix of the other, 533
# generated lines, 533 committed" — pointed away from the cause, because
# `str::lines` strips the `\r` that the byte comparison had just tripped on.
#
# So: LF in the working tree on every platform. `text=auto` still detects
# binary content and leaves it alone; the explicit rules below say so for the
# fixtures where a heuristic should not be the argument.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures, named rather than detected.
*.png   binary
*.bin   binary
*.rom   binary
*.nes   binary
*.gb    binary
*.img   binary
*.fd    binary
*.qcow2 binary
*.wasm  binary
*.tar   binary
*.gz    binary
*.xz    binary
